        question: "What surface do fencing pistes need?",
        answer: "Metallic (conductive) pistes for electric scoring — typically aluminum or copper-alloy mesh surfaces laid over the floor — or the sport flooring beneath where scoring uses other systems. The base floor needs to be perfectly flat and level (fencers feel every irregularity through thin shoes), with the right grip for explosive lunges and enough resilience for long sessions. The conductivity and flatness requirements make the floor a genuine engineered assembly.",
